# Every path the fork changes relative to Compose's source, and the content it has there.
#
# The fork is thisisthepy/compose-multiplatform-core-extended, and build-compose.sh pins
# one commit of it. These lines are what that commit holds at each path it changed
# relative to the upstream revision it starts from (JetBrains release/1.11, 73ac849):
# the Linux targets, the native text context menu, the version it publishes as, and the
# design systems under extended/design-systems with the workflow that builds them.
# scripts/tests/compose-fork.test.sh reads the pinned commit's tree and checks every line,
# so a pin that loses one of these changes fails there and not in a renderer build an
# hour later.
#
# Format: the git blob hash the path must hold, or `-` where the path must be absent,
# then the path. Moving the pin means regenerating this from the new commit, which
# means deciding, path by path, that each change is still there:
#
#   git diff --raw --no-renames --no-abbrev <upstream base> <pinned commit> |
#       awk '{ print ($5 == "D" ? "-" : $4), $6 }'
